=='''Strategy'''==
While this stage seems like it might be annoying on paper, most of the major threats spawn on a timer. As such, it's fairly easy to rush the stage with strong [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|Rushers]] like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion Cat]], [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]], and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev/Bullet Train Cat]]. It's recommended to time Maglev/Bullet Train so that it hits the first Gabriel and/or Doge Dark for a burst of cash, letting Awakened Bahamut hit the field faster. Bringing a pair of small Attack Up [[Cat Combo]]s (typically some combination of [[Sister Act (Combo)|Sister Act]], [[Tiny Ancient Hunt (Combo)|Tiny Ancient Hunt]], and/or [[Brave Cutter (Combo)|Brave Cutter]]) is advised to make the rush more reliable, especially at higher magnifications.

If you struggle to keep the Dober P.D at the base, then bring [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Glass Cat]] to stun him. Be sure to leave deployment space for Glass Cat and be careful when timing it so that it doesn't hit a peon, especially if Zoge manages to burrow.

==Trivia==
*Unlike other part II [[Gauntlet]]s, this gauntlet starts at Lv.1 rather than Lv.11. Strangely enough, this anomaly doesn't appear in the original Japanese version, only the English one.

